<article class="agustos-container">
  <p class="type-h4" style="color: var(--signal); margin-top: 0;">Rails adapter · v3</p>
  <h1 class="type-hero-md">A typography-first Rails monolith.</h1>
  <p class="type-hero-deck">
    Same registry, same rhythm, same publisher mark. Rails owns the application;
    the design system owns the visual grammar.
  </p>

  <p class="hero-links">
    <%= link_to "Read the design system", "#", class: "hero-link hero-link--primary" %>
    <%= link_to "Start a page", "#", class: "hero-link hero-link--secondary" %>
  </p>

  <hr class="type-divider">

  <h2 class="type-h2">Editorial content</h2>
  <p class="type-body">
    Use the same typography tokens inside ERB, Rails partials, ViewComponent,
    or content-rendered HTML. Brand color remains a signal, not decoration.
  </p>
</article>
